-- title:
--   Diamond operators act trivially after localisation at the residual eigensystem
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, meaning its base change to $\overline{k}$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p\in S$, let $N\neq 0$, and let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$ and $p\nmid r-1$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra away from $S$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}\,S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the Hecke generators indexed by primes outside $S$ not dividing $N$), and assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell\in\mathrm{nonunits}(P)$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$), one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ in $k[X]$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be nonzero naturals and $\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_t\in k$; put $L=N\bigl(\prod_i q_i\bigr)r$ and $H_r=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/r)^\times\bigr)$, and let $V_L$ be the cohomology carrier $H^1(L,H_r;\mathcal O)$. Assume the operators attached to the generators indexed by $\mathrm{Gen}(L,S,t)$ commute pairwise on $V_L$. Form the Hecke data on $V_L$ whose residual character is built from $\theta$ and $\alpha$, and let $v\mapsto \bar v$ denote its localisation map $V_L\to \mathrm{ML}$, the localisation at the complement of the prime $\mathfrak m_\theta$ of the associated free polynomial algebra. The assertion is that for every $u\in(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ and every $v\in V_L$ one has $\overline{\langle u\rangle v}=\bar v$, where $\langle u\rangle$ is the $\mathcal O$-endomorphism of $V_L$ induced by a chosen lift of $u$ to $\Gamma_0(L)$.
--
--   This is the statement that there are no congruences with forms of non-trivial nebentypus at the auxiliary prime $r$ for the Taylor–Wiles modules at level $N\prod q_i$ intersected with $\Gamma_1(r)$: the localisation at the residual eigensystem, which prescribes no diamond operator, is unchanged by the diamond operators $\langle u\rangle$, the hypothesis $p\nmid r-1$ being what rules out non-trivial characters of $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$ of $p$-power order. It is used in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_linearEquiv_ML_HR_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_linearEquiv_ML_HR_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq) to compare the Taylor–Wiles module at auxiliary level with the one cut out at level $N\prod q_i$.
